		{"id":"46af5e7dce82f743","type":"text","text":"- [Memory Efficient Continual Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.03866)\n    - neurips 2024 workshop paper. continual learning for clip models. They used a fixed buffer memory size and designed a better objective function for CL. Used moving average to estimate summations for the contrastive loss. \n    - added dynamic weight scaling for previous classes based on high their losses are . Higher the loss , higher the weight. They got great improvements in memory. over previous methods.\n- ","x":408,"y":-3141,"width":792,"height":1001},
